cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PRL-8-53 target hypotheses: a bounded evidence audit and limited docking checks"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hasan Ugur"
    family-names: "Yildirim"
    alias: "Rolf"
    affiliation: "Lasell University, Newton, MA, USA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uguryildirim24/prl-8-53-targets"
url: "https://github.com/uguryildirim24/prl-8-53-targets"
abstract: >-
  An evidence audit and limited computational docking checks of the molecular-target
  hypotheses for PRL-8-53, an experimental compound with historical behavioural
  reports but no established mechanism. No binding target is established. The ACC2
  pilot was stopped when its native-ligand redocking control failed, so no
  PRL-8-53/ACC2 score exists; a SERT reference pilot passed its control and
  produced exploratory, uncalibrated PRL-8-53 poses. The result is an auditable
  shortlist of hypotheses with explicit failure evidence, not target confirmation.
keywords:
  - PRL-8-53
  - molecular docking
  - AutoDock Vina
  - target deconvolution
  - reproducibility
  - negative result
  - computational pharmacology
